- Story & Context: The legend of Juna’s reckless Flux-Runs and the uniquely savage, detuned sound that emerged from her resurrected Hammond grew across the Scavenge Desert, passed between trading caravans, until it was said that on the longest day, the Detuned Solstice, the very air in the canyons hummed with the memory of sacrificed circuits and the triumphant, almost sacred roar of her re-bent Hammond, now a living, metallic deity of desert resilience. "Every glitch a prayer, every hum a hymn."
